  <!--
    Danish. The proof that the pipeline switches at all - see notes/localisation.md.

    A key missing here falls back to the neutral file rather than failing, so a partial translation
    is a mixed page and never a broken one. That is what makes Phase B able to proceed a page at a
    time.

    Danish plurals take the same two forms as English (én printer / to printere), so the One/Other
    pair is enough here. It is not enough for every language, which is why Plural.Format is a seam
    rather than a string concatenation.
  -->
